esigner — `chkEnableAttack` (the designer had an unnamed `checkBox1` with text \"Enable Atack\") and `txtHitCount` (missing entirely). Changes, all in `psdisabled/MuProxy2/MuProxy2/MainForm.Designer.cs`: 1. **Renamed `checkBox1` → `chkEnableAttack`** (all 11 occurrences: instantiation, `groupBox5.Controls.Add`, property block, field declaration) — it's the \"Enable Attack\" checkbox in the Attack Config group, exactly what `MainForm.cs:172,185,188` expects. 2. **Added `txtHitCount` + `label5` (\"Hits\")** to groupBox5, following the existing label/textbox pattern: - instantiations (after `txtDelay`) - `groupBox5.Controls.Add(label5)` / `Controls.Add(txtHitCount)` (Designer.cs:653–654) - property blocks: label at (11, 217), textbox at (57, 213) — directly below the Delay row, default text `\"1\"` matching `AttackService.HitCount`'s default of 1 - field declarations `private Label label5; private TextBox txtHitCount;` Verification: - Workspace diagnostics: **0 errors, 0 warnings** - `dotnet build MuProxy2.csproj`: **Build succeeded, 0 Warning(s), 0 Error(s)**\n- **Tools:** read_file, search_files, rename, edit_file, run_command, glob","vector":[0.07609153,-0.0064764246,-0.16237248,-0.0044855815,0.06843267,-0.03256462,0.015255011,0.06443447,-0.024200605,-0.06548725,-0.038437653,0.006508274,0.05392137,-0.011090581,-0.037337724,-0.067704014,0.012755146,-0.00024668738,-0.04570872,0.01043796,0.019682227,-0.060186155,-0.017853998,-0.030790767,0.087114,0.07078601,0.0146388365,0.02053135,-0.033817012,-0.013497864,0.04209071,0.024853608,-0.00903184,-0.015800107,-0.022300772,-0.028294327,0.03760237,-0.0039848667,-0.03901575,0.047821917,0.051947087,0.012720578,-0.0009238422,-0.06852714,-0.04065186,-0.019034952,0.05980797,0.043113787,0.05078525,-0.08824079,0.022154227,-0.056844566,0.053928245,-0.008413477,0.058128137,0.008855312,-0.045084566,0.03590509,0.009596345,-0.06362269,0.037045732,0.09158114,0.008852534,0.034027673,0.0031446451,0.016297134,-0.02899469,0.031119525,-0.037605