123603,-0.029767755,-0.039162032,-0.019691722,-0.008636832,0.042718872,-0.010990869,0.023544095,0.01515291,-0.0288594,0.02064803,-0.030823063,0.076601416,-0.048978824,0.028297523,-0.015497576,-0.028967774,-0.020991966,-0.023257948,-0.042646565,-0.0060112285,-0.010083117,0.020946946,0.024038402,0.0018572522,0.03543137,-0.032106854,-0.0045274985,-0.025421133,0.065822296,0.0015679348,-0.06605127,0.0041741356,0.006650687,-0.039982326,0.0038461946,-0.035439257,0.012563193,-0.042195696,0.0019760188,-0.008789377,-0.0019208038,0.069184564,-0.012196141,-0.0442014,-0.041356508,0.018863888,-0.060575582,0.01282374,-0.04748367,-0.0052912533,0.002172776,0.0116756465,0.025964405,0.0062157926,0.014129766,0.012255753,0.014421362,0.0038451948,0.011403341,0.0034582475,-0.03776583,0.011477499,-0.043520298,-0.014157929,0.027414272,0.006066591,0.12235155,0.040175207,0.0036355327,-0.04614041,0.060742695,0.011170353,0.021155179,-0.046414793,0.00024148317,0.0050995857],"hash":"14d27cba:1937","model":"nomic-embed-text:latest","archived":true},{"uri":"file:///f%3A/blackrockmu/.novamind/memory/session-log.md","text":"## 2026-11-13T23:18:08.526Z\n- **User:** eai\n- **Outcome:** Tudo verificado e consistente. A correção está completa e **deployada**. ## O que estava errado (causa raiz do DC) O C116 real capturado (linha 13 do log): ``` C1 16 F4 03 3134352E3233392E3134392E3834 00 F9 4D B3 │ │ │ └────────── \"145.239.149.84\" (16B) ──────┘ └─ porta 45901 (LE) │ │ └ charID (2B) │ └ header └ C1 16 ``` Duas premissas erradas no código antigo: 1. **Escaneava `FE 2B` (forma cifrada)** — mas o login server manda o C116 **em claro** (`C1 16`). Nunca casava → porta nunca detectada. 2. **Lia a porta no offset 4-5** — mas ela está no **offset 20** (`4D B3` = 45901). Como a porta real (45901) está **fora** do range hardcoded (55901–55950), o fallback não ajudava → `127.0.0.1:45901` sem listener → **DC**. ## O que mudei | Arquivo | Correção | |---------|----------| | `gg_bypass2/src/PacketSniffer.cpp:372` | `