96117,-0.010371954,-0.010568666,0.07005157,-0.028225843,-0.06875565,-0.0006389048,0.017349398,-0.038210604,0.02441009,-0.0008615108,-0.010361979,-0.013434539,0.0010404859,-0.014245245,-0.04541976,0.05353081,-0.028789392,-0.0411127,-0.035086825,-0.031100387,-0.05639534,0.0072534136,-0.058159288,0.012578792,-0.044129986,0.0126725985,0.01258403,0.02889287,-0.028929992,0.017789863,0.027870933,-0.007374477,0.044730403,0.0078088553,-0.067693256,-0.041786157,-0.022479055,-0.010519819,-0.00014414413,0.0153320795,0.13863301,0.019492941,0.03231342,-0.027051453,0.035434045,0.028662845,-0.025186425,-0.044648867,-0.060827717,-0.045888983],"hash":"7b27aa5:441","model":"nomic-embed-text:latest","archived":true},{"uri":"file:///f%3A/blackrockmu/.novamind/memory/session-log.md","text":"## 2026-11-14T02:57:37.618Z\n- **User:** esta funcionando lindamente agora... entretanto parece que o range nao esta.\n- **Outcome:** Pronto. Resumo do que foi feito: ## Bug do range — corrigido **Causa raiz:** o \"spray ±1\" leftover em `AttackSingleMobThread` (AttackModule.cpp:365-367) atacava `entityIndex-1` e `entityIndex+1` a cada hit, **ignorando o range**. Era um hack da época do bug do XOR 0xEFF5 — agora que o alvo exato funciona, era puro desperdício. **Evidência no log (18:49:59):** padrão repetido `0x0013, 0x0012, 0x0011` — três índices adjacentes atacados em ciclo, mesmo com `range=8.0` configurado. **Correção:** agora ataca somente o `entityIndex` exato. O range já é aplicado corretamente pelo Watcher (que só mantém monstros dentro do `g_SessionRange * TILE_SIZE` no `g_MonsterMap`, atualizado a cada 500ms) — o check `alive` da thread é, na prática, o check de range. ## Bug bônus — deploy do build.bat falhava silenciosamente Encontrei ao verificar o timestamp: o `byp.dll` no diretório do jogo **não tinha sido atualizado** pelo build. Causa: `timeout /t 2` falha imediatamente quando o stdin é redirecionado (`ERROR: Input redirection is not supported`), eliminando a espera de 2s — o `copy` rodava enquanto o main.exe ainda segurava o lock do byp.dll → \"Acesso negado\" escondido pelo `>nul`, e o \"DEPLOY OK\" ecoava de qualquer jeito. **Correção (build.bat:40-42):** `timeout` → `ping -n 3 127.0.0.1` (funciona com redirecionamento) e removi o `>nul` dos `copy` para falhas ficarem visíveis. ## Deploy - Build OK: `dist\\byp.dll` 18:55:07 (69.120 bytes) - Copiado manualmente para `F:\\blackrockmu\\byp.dll` (con…\n- **Tools:** search_files, read_file, edit_file","vector":[0.04637503,0.05509505,-0.17693138,-0.0054869624,0.071995646,-0.025138251,0.042072125,0.022044616,-0.04760719,-0.0090844575,-0.008416483,0.044430096,0.0682361,-0.021609051,0.0011438676,-0.03305476,-0.002509091,-0.03332752,-0.037939757,0.020001838,0.023232004,-0.026428182,-0.025853349,-0.055670634,0.07841353,0.03977477,0.00834548,0.064103395,-0.019484283,0.0143348025,0.042436004,0.064916775,-0.013048213,-0.019613601,0.014021497,-0.050267026,0.032911718,-0.024804696,0.008572468,0.013086044,0.018488264,-0.049775485,0.018501308,-0.008528587,0.030184446,0.033454597,0.061125398,0.052678365,0.05992382,-0.08017619,0.008174298,0.020759486,0.013581009,-0.020947715,0.07812062,0.051435404,-0.049427915,0.023844332,0.06224969,-0.04149366,0.090778865,0.03233548,-0.026338883,0.057804156,-0.000013500509,-0.017851245,-0.03534066,-0.0007284528,-0.035268776,-0.012897162,0.04814206,-0.026445678,-0.018979736,0.008540932,-0.028219992,0.016073385,-0.026914448,-0.02984111,0.009279249,0.04064703,-0.020109246,0.03789678,0.06257954,-0.037689462,0.04766774,0.031001871,-0.039850555,0.011021601,-0.056039494,0.08692917,0.010613067,-0.0303558,0.038450178,-0.033624355,-0.044788048,0.013981021,-0.04355023,-0.0024004432,-0.01313453,-0.04168066,-0.0329486,0.023828944,0.018433869,-0.020783637,0.0030618452,0.052550968,0.02344039,-0.022611434,-0.057812184,-0.00037559075,0.02430985,0.0041348725,-0.0017906453,-0.07257255,0.013023413,-0.03445156,0.06502138,-0.01888971,0.008924606,0.028191017,-0.043966517,-0.022448031,-0.0073282835,0.