yStart = hdrSize + 3`, apontando para o byte **ListType** (`data[5]`) em vez do primeiro SkillEntry (`data[6]`). A documentação OpenMU confirma o layout: ``` [4]=Count(0xFE/0xFF) [5]=ListType [6+]=SkillEntry[] (4B: Index, Number LE, Level) ``` | | Antes (errado) | Depois (correto) | |---|---|---| | entryStart | `data[5]` (ListType) | `data[6]` (SkillEntry) | | SkillIndex | `0x00` | **`0x08`** | | SkillNumber | `0x1308` | **`0x0013`** | Por isso **nunca** houve entrada `SKILLMAP` no log — o mapa era populado com skillNumber `0x1308` (absurdo) em vez de `0x0013`. **Mudanças em `SkillMap.cpp`:** - Linhas 37-41: `entryStart = hdrSize + 4` (pula o ListType) nos dois caminhos (add/remove e lista) - Linha 40: lê `listType` e usa como desempate (2 = remove) - Linhas 31-36: comentário corrigido — o BlackRock **envia sim** o F3 11 **Validação:** repl confirmou que o parser corrigido extrai `SkillIndex=0x08, SkillNumber=0x0013` do pacote real do capture. Parser F3 E2 já estava correto (skillNumber LE em off+0, level em off+20). **Build:** SUCESSO, sem erros (apenas warnings pré-existentes de `inet_ntoa`/`/EHsc`). **Deploy:** `F:\\blackrockmu\\byp.dll` atualizado às 19:43:44. **Próximo passo (pendente):** reinicia o jogo e confere o log — deve aparecer `SKILLMAP ADD: index=0x08 number=0x0013` quando o servidor enviar a skill list.\n- **Tools:** edit_file, read_file, repl, manage_todos, run_command","vector":[0.055925228,0.02191618,-0.15851551,-0.07721626,0.069231585,-0.03472809,0.04555881,0.04355412,-0.018835094,-0.040195227,-0.06387231,0.033693656,0.06583678,-0.006657674,0.025934462,-0.002022389,-0.029128764,-0.051187124,-0.010731739,0.039642196,-0.0037821364,-0.049522568,0.00057314354,-0.024434268,0.070842914,0.018356455,-0.008756359,0.026625503,-0.0108829755,-0.0034467422,0.015831264,0.0350592,-0.0011920998,-0.06528238,-0.016557524,-0.054380387,0.041936208,-0.016508639,0.002704184,0.021696435,0.013019648,-0.049913798,-0.027677253,-0.010226481,0.025781825,0.018917628,0.066584