:"nomic-embed-text:latest","archived":true},{"uri":"file:///f%3A/blackrockmu/.novamind/memory/session-log.md","text":"## 2026-11-14T13:10:29.543Z\n- **User:** caralho eu nao quero que vc analise a porra do log, quero que vc adicione a desgraca do log. recebeu um pacote crypted ? exibe a porra da versao decrypted na msm linha, para facilitar as analises o caralho. faz essa porra agora e para de ficar analisando infinito\n- **Outcome:** Feito. O byp.dll foi rebuildado e deployado em `F:\\blackrockmu\\byp.dll`. **O que mudei:** 1. **`Logger.h`** — declarei `LogPacketDual(tag, dir, raw, rawLen, dec, decLen)`. 2. **`Logger.cpp`** — implementei `LogPacketDual`: loga `hex=<raw crypted> dec=<decrypted>` na mesma linha. Se `dec==nullptr`, só loga `hex=<raw>` (comportamento antigo). 3. **`PacketSniffer.cpp`** (`LogRaw`) — pra pacotes do game server, agora chama `LogPacketDual` com o raw (`data`) e o decryptado (`decrypted`). Pra sockets não-GS (sem chave), continua `LogPacket` (só raw). **Formato novo no log (pacotes GS):** ``` [2026-11-14 04:44:05.608] [PACKETSNIFFER] [RECV] len=8 hex=<Crypted> dec=<Decrypted> ``` **Formato antigo (não-GS, sem chave):** ``` [2026-11-14 04:44:05.608] [PACKETSNIFFER] [RECV] len=8 hex=<Raw> ``` O build.bat já matou o `main.exe`. **Reinicia o game** que o novo byp.dll carrega e o log já sai com as duas versões na mesma linha.\n- **Tools:** search_files, glob, edit_file, run_command, read_file","vector":[0.050364714,0.052890338,-0.15157714,-0.06590161,0.056455262,-0.1081122,0.028203914,0.01351696,-0.099912934,-0.05475563,-0.07922112,0.042000607,0.061300922,-0.049972042,0.0077082333,-0.049907584,-0.028358003,-0.04657702,-0.040636174,0.0035060253,0.030886335,-0.039952952,0.012896531,-0.046086926,0.066109285,-0.017738122,0.00761805,0.04678081,-0.043980308,-0.01869972,0.058717728,-0.009598349,-0.0073033287,-0.016858032,-0.024860231,-0.06304593,0.00990996,-0.0147045,-0.0030449678,-0.015931245,0.028755024,-0.019772721,0.024721317,-0.021481626,-0.000811