o send foi desativado. O jogo está rodando. **Agora faz assim:** 1. No jogo, posiciona perto de um monstro. 2. Faz um **ataque de skill manual** (o mesmo skill que a DLL usa, `0x003C`, se possível — assim a comparação fica direta). 3. Me avisa quando fez. Quando o BP disparar, o x64dbg pausa **exatamente** na função que monta o pacote `C1 07 19`. Aí eu leio: - `[ebp+8]` e `[ebp+0C]` → ponteiro da **entidade alvo** e o skill - A memória do monstro (index/slot/id) → para correlacionar com os bytes `E7 C3 E2 CF` do log - O stack completo no momento certo Com isso a gente descobre **de fato** como o jogo codifica o index (é o `0x02E8` direto? XOR? offset?) e a ordem exata dos bytes — sem mais chute. Faz o ataque e me dá um sinal.\n- **Tools:** mcp_tool","vector":[0.027994856,0.054837678,-0.15823942,-0.05004609,0.05529215,-0.057390224,0.066626236,0.004541884,-0.08297886,-0.0046403063,-0.08907056,-0.0032903985,0.027127167,-0.027860595,0.0013037378,-0.048396144,-0.018683117,-0.058646142,-0.040817954,0.043543983,-0.0137439445,-0.019634953,-0.051611155,-0.028882777,0.06845887,0.0017972818,-0.008643157,0.03942527,-0.0347067,0.008961886,0.015289861,0.0122725675,-0.029283045,-0.02544753,0.00069442915,-0.028427519,0.024849547,-0.021298373,-0.013493973,-0.038197003,-0.026890391,-0.042796478,0.043566123,-0.008052077,0.016760258,0.043220546,0.026359072,0.0441181,0.042665467,-0.033602428,0.035585023,0.013053992,-0.0055547315,-0.067185566,0.10470218,0.05298388,-0.04307232,0.010730134,0.052288648,-0.028137337,0.09483488,0.022101806,0.029731547,0.10498901,0.051827695,-0.015385776,-0.042086467,0.029097803,-0.068095595,-0.0142006995,0.030372255,-0.0055801603,0.031963192,0.013137748,-0.018673245,-0.011120357,-0.034767352,-0.029399091,-0.004898117,-0.03449364,0.028050369,-0.0067063677,0.10224616,-0.025352687,0.0019064143,-0.027368894,-0.0381588,0.01346935,-0.057051495,0.07083902,-0.043397624,-0.012387971,0.038278632,0.015230937,-0.04003351,0.028324584,-0.038243357,0.030582096,-0.060449548,