al + pacotes) vai para `gg_bypass2.log` - **`src/dllmain.cpp`** — `InitializeLogging` monta apenas o caminho único - **`src/AttackModule.cpp`** — removidos 4 pontos de log de ataque normal (`ComputeDirection`, `SendAttack` por hit, diagnóstico redundante em `SendConfiguredAttack`, log por ciclo do Dispatcher). Restam: ataques de skill, eventos de lifecycle (Watcher/Dispatcher, add/remove de monstro) e diagnósticos sob demanda (DUMP/HEXDUMP/SCANVALUE/SCANSLOT/DIRSCAN) ## Fase 2 — Formato do sniffer ✅ - **`src/Logger.cpp`** — `LogPacketDual` imprime `dec=<decoded> enc=<wire>` (decifrado primeiro, wire depois) - **`src/PacketSniffer.cpp`**: - `TryDecodeC3C4` — decifra C3/C4 (Layer-1 XOR+sub **e** SM) para mostrar o plaintext real - `LogRaw` — usa `TryDecodeC3C4` e chama `LogPacketDual` com as duas formas - `HookSend` — removidos EBP, stack trace, hex dump, bloco SM debug - `HookRecv`/`HookWSASend`/`WSARecv` — logs de ruído removidos - `ProcessSkillQueue` — passo-a-passo removido nos caminhos BUILDER e MANUAL - `InjectToServer` (~linha 1410) — adicionado `LogPacketDual(\"PACKETSNIFFER\", \"SEND\", ...)` entre a criptografia e o `TrueSend`, já que injetados não passam pelo `HookSend` ## Verificação - Build via `build.bat`: **…\n- **Tools:** edit_file, search_files, run_command, read_file, manage_todos","vector":[0.025752297,0.028371708,-0.15092896,-0.042274777,0.044038463,-0.090496875,0.03832077,0.011041807,-0.058917727,-0.059299774,-0.073454544,-0.018225849,0.08632121,0.0054335487,0.04625299,-0.029281508,-0.00008547001,-0.056773454,-0.057865445,0.008245093,0.023944058,-0.048932143,0.017861348,-0.016962018,0.061073527,0.06469986,0.0076993,0.07496645,-0.05006123,-0.023577172,0.054151624,0.022465227,-0.01667161,-0.042814698,-0.0025814842,-0.054626696,0.008958509,-0.077821575,-0.016200319,0.00022683348,0.018271042,-0.05040874,0.012403184,-0.048131157,0.020235669,0.028069079,0.065489925,-0.002530562,0.068455786,-0.10458071,0.007044275,0.041396253,-0.010486302,-0.04667516,0.1