 deixado um comentário documentando o endereço do jogo (`0x998490`) e o motivo da remoção (DecKey zero no Obj1) - **`src/include/SimpleModulusCipher.h`**: declaração `NativeDecrypt` removida; `NativeEncrypt` mantido (usado no self-test de `Initialize`) ## O que o log vai mostrar agora (por pacote C3/C4) ``` [PACKETSNIFFER] SEND C3 24 bytes [C3 18 C6 DC ...] [PACKETSNIFFER] SEND stack: Main.dll+0xBB3DE ... [SMOD] SM input bytes (22): [C6 DC 37 B7 ...] [SMOD] DecryptBlock #27: src=[...] ring=[...] checksum OK [PACKETSNIFFER] SEND C3 decrypt: OK decLen=11 [PACKETSNIFFER] SEND C3>C1 decoded: [C1 0C 0E ...] dk=0A ``` ## Verificação - Build via `build.bat`: **sucesso**, `byp.dll` copiado pra `F:\\blackrockmu\\` - Diagnósticos: **0 erros** nos dois arquivos editados O ruído de `DecryptBlock` (ring/slot a cada bloco) continua lá — se quiser, ainda posso condensa como ofereci antes (chaves logadas uma vez só + blocos subsequentes só com plaintext/checksum). É só dizer.\n- **Tools:** search_files, edit_file, run_command","vector":[0.05555936,0.036833655,-0.15342385,-0.053920608,0.057436053,-0.0812344,0.047081087,-0.004482372,-0.02586069,-0.073474884,-0.10531394,0.026477573,0.046665695,-0.007363782,0.035158012,-0.004014284,0.0038116288,-0.05261675,-0.02272832,0.04278683,0.026472058,-0.03907364,-0.045278035,-0.0024218955,0.07868688,0.020317012,-0.007973751,0.033667445,-0.041091073,0.010738412,0.051645912,0.00026994586,-0.0066467198,-0.03785909,-0.021588536,-0.041904144,0.03685458,-0.027842192,-0.007423664,-0.011076353,0.01246466,-0.018291619,0.005233814,-0.018760903,0.027088638,0.045059144,0.045206446,-0.0031884457,0.05826827,-0.107170194,0.016825609,0.010189778,0.030387277,-0.04067141,0.08165567,0.014141748,-0.05800665,0.03703195,0.010196478,-0.035348624,0.07056623,0.023411937,-0.02956194,0.0347292,0.0027501348,-0.00014529262,-0.04906136,0.056220155,-0.036198393,-0.0003888677,0.04510811,-0.031004183,-0.00029698265,0.008105091,0.0066694175,-0.0014005343,-0.039772525,-0.04471837