isar o que temos. A situação: **Fato 1:** No builder (`0x59C725`), `[EBP-0x1C]` = **0x3C** (índice bruto) **Fato 2:** No pacote (send), skill = **0xE7C3** Isso confirma o que você disse — o skill ID **sofre transformação**. O caminho é a tabela em `0x59C299`: ```asm movzx eax, word [edx+ecx*2+0x78] ; wire ID da tabela ``` O problema: quando eu li a flag `[0x081C0398]`, estava 0. Mas provavelmente ela está **ativa durante o cast** e reseta depois. Meu BP em `0x59C725` deve ter pegado um **auto-attack diferente** (o jogo casta rapidinho). **Próximo passo:** BP em `0x59C2B8` (onde `[EBP-0x1C]` é escrito) com condição pra só pegar quando o valor for ≠ 0x3C. Ou melhor: BP direto em `0x59C299` (a instrução da tabela) — se bater, a tabela está ativa. Quer que eu monte o BP em `0x59C299`? Se bater, eu leio: - `ECX` = índice usado - `EDX` = base da tabela - `EAX` = wire ID resultante (deve ser 0xE7C3) Assim mapeamos a tabela inteira.\n- **Tools:** mcp_tool","vector":[0.04879069,0.045289457,-0.13800345,-0.015778927,0.09458882,-0.035078004,0.06484709,0.03537832,-0.065871276,-0.015197507,-0.046980433,0.041495107,0.07084477,-0.030489208,0.015091001,-0.034212977,-0.0010868545,-0.05927203,-0.02958113,0.053821295,0.037907857,-0.0070820185,-0.053641755,-0.027748263,0.09930117,-0.030625327,-0.013625602,0.04512361,-0.074473046,-0.041852273,0.010304196,0.03133758,0.017148048,-0.034951344,-0.03062709,-0.041249312,0.041808236,0.031653434,-0.029262204,-0.006571132,0.009334094,-0.09399215,0.0022335974,0.0012870214,-0.0038775504,0.026071606,0.05546359,0.044007767,0.033231646,-0.06850026,0.036108337,-0.001820247,0.0042094295,-0.041589815,0.080233574,0.022882614,-0.041090786,0.0057658344,0.031002203,0.002782832,0.06564366,-0.0017075524,-0.03685971,0.12541226,0.012231089,0.022708962,-0.0170229,0.021991525,-0.04484934,0.005444975,0.031884577,-0.030888148,0.015917856,0.022580307,-0.013633279,-0.011390228,-0.03820739,-0.057934742,0.04570726,0.01512344,0.011350419,0.019304633,0.10781752,-0.0378106