 (o payload passa por um XOR encadeado em PacketManager::XorData): vira C1 07 19 00 3C 02 77. Agora vou conferir se o servidor aceita 7 bytes e tentar abrir o C3. Errei antes: o C1 07 19 da sua captura é o pacote de skill de verdade, e o servidor aceita. C1 07 19 E7 C3 E2 50 O payload de todo C1 vindo do cliente passa por um XOR encadeado. Ele começa no byte 3 e o head 0x19 fica intacto. O servidor desfaz em CPacketManager::XorData (PacketManager.…\n- **Outcome:** **Não.** O skill C1 07 19 **não** passa por SimpleModulus/C3. O caminho real (validado na captura) é o mesmo do ataque normal 0x11: ``` plaintext ─► XorData[3,7) (XOR encadeado) ─► Layer-1 (XOR+sub 0x36/0x07) ─► wire (C1 puro) ``` Evidências: 1. **A captura decodifica sem SM.** `C1 07 19 E7 C3 E2 50` aparece no wire como **C1** e o XorData sozinho devolve `00 3C 02 77` (skill 60, monstro 631). Se SimpleModulus estivesse por cima, o XorData não recuperaria isso — precisaria da chave SM primeiro. 2. **O servidor aceita C1 direto.** Protocol.cpp:101 — `case 0x19: CGSkillAttackRecv(...)` no switch de C1. Não há caminho C3 para skill. 3. **O C3 0D [11 bytes] das capturas é outro pacote** (SM, pequeno, ainda não decifrado — falta o Dec1.dat). Não é o skill. O que o código faz agora, após a correção: - `SendSkillAttack` (AttackModule.cpp:167) monta o plaintext `[C1][07][19][skillH][skillL][indexH][indexL]` e chama `InjectC1Attack` → **XorData[3,7) → Layer-1 → send** (PacketSniffer.cpp:1676). - O caminho antigo **SM → C3** (`SKILL_TYPE_MANUAL` na fila do HookSend) **não é mais usado pelo skill** — ele era baseado no misread do \"0xE7C3\" (na verdade era o `00 3C` cifrado pelo XorData). O mecanismo de fila ficou no PacketSniffer mas o skill não passa mais por ele. Resumindo a diferença: | | Antes (errado) | Agora (correto) | |---|---|---| | Caminho | C1 payload → SM → C3 0D → Layer-1 | plaintext → XorData → Layer-1 → **C1** | | Layout | intercalado `[idxH][skillH][idxL][skillL]` + 0xEFF…\n- **Tools:** search_files, list_directory, read_file, edit_file, glob, git, write_file","vector":[0.056389153,0.0017933103,-0.1553375,-0.056432746,0.043921478,-0.0583642,0.054644015,0.009518603,-0.04743791,-0.02071509,-0.07351043,-0.0329914,0.06216791,-0.057367705,0.011384759,-0.02968695,-0.021913223,-0.03916653,-0.039452266,0.035020724,0.040768065,-0.033889454,-0.008696033,-0.023921525,0.07877669,0.033263326,-0.018322483,0.024779545,-0.07146163,-0.014589946,0.055073164,-0.003991003,0.0036115414,-0.06765241,0.015581449,-0.038147453,0.036317855,-0.00859158,-0.04285976,0.0015464408,0.024236817,-0.051725034,0.02859288,-0.014181802,0.0132378405,0.003184843,0.034941524,0.016899753,0.047581486,-0.111377396,0.022099271,0.020745466,-0.012876311,-0.035649676,0.071628064,0.024924565,-0.02034883,-0.008011861,0.009013909,-0.06319862,0.07956014,0.006846075,0.007685706,0.07603233,0.011306104,-0.013418536,-0.050184235,0.046822146,-0.051655553,-0.0074680396,0.06614397,-0.018159464,0.018480903,0.011543822,-0.0029579145,-0.042112567,-0.05729327,-0.036090624,-0.017823212,-0.037819214,0.013770441,-0.018353872,0.0773696,-0.044444665,0.045697663,-0.012775873,-0.03632916,-0.016770395,-0.02699286,0.0849448,-0.0053883553,-0.025628652,0.025586916,0.01791154,-0.042094655,0.011599691,-0.010486633,0.040799994,-0.008749746,-0.020600129,-0.023103071,-0.018204087,0.015385029,-0.029214256,-0.0015646074,0.060747556,0.0071527986,0.006698056,0.0023699359,-0.0029445789,-0.0058039105,0.011117888,-0.036436222,-0.04321357,0.07327517,-0.022224821,0.050921418,-0.021840837,0.0027898753,0.03385537,-0.042524166,-0.012689866,0.007991345,0.046754062,0.06918214,0.017605795,0.0066202194,0.028553925,0.036734693,-0.07578457,-0.0038173168,-0.00601278,-0.034996983,0.03416053,0.012590561,0.021296611,-0.021853486,0.005697707,0.06031097,0.04641521,0.0017675103,0.0027041712,0.028892253,0.0017016287,0.038170237,-0.05676388,0.0076197945,-0.020188672,-0.047389347,-0.029377416,0.040884327,0.0044844956,-0.022407878,0.055297155,-0.003773111,-0.006228001