,0.03909163,-0.0077719307,-0.018683646,-0.0269154,0.02119723,-0.0694756,0.063186035,0.04667126,0.012806169,0.026822396,0.06697291,0.08716346,0.060751267,-0.009656205,0.039728917,-0.043196857,0.01913582,0.0011819409,-0.05035654,-0.052052666,0.039074834,-0.0007444075,-0.016363569,-0.0051267473,0.021732539,-0.0019643097,0.046077836,-0.013193386,-0.07304889,-0.06339588,0.011377,0.06340013,0.018228935,0.014162443,0.06007973,-0.02370152,0.08401783,-0.005861335,-0.044165093,-0.014767651,-0.009067833,-0.008521613,0.036470562,0.054596666,0.00906157,-0.039979406,0.019790614,-0.033766165,-0.011398673,-0.017985975,0.005363339,-0.010102951,-0.0011453856,-0.05136678,-0.022096312,0.008064292,0.0008344517,-0.023293285,0.01145282,0.048854623,-0.0184078,0.028237173,-0.013920255,0.021969788,-0.024459925,0.030951267,-0.033517238,-0.04439877,-0.038501006,-0.019625483,-0.052014217,0.022298655,-0.05208801,-0.005900852,0.0146607645,0.012148651,0.004345006,-0.032648273,0.022659669,0.012933109,0.005631819,0.040148757,-0.05045621,0.028127752,0.04077399,0.01581042,7.1020855e-7,-0.018478567,0.02524242,-0.023685623,0.020558083,-0.030878754,-0.052860923,0.051390704,0.02806132,0.04515608,-0.0016210171,-0.023005538,-0.041451342,-0.02644643,-0.03661299,0.041846145,0.0011894858,-0.0055635856,-0.023703102,0.0014624698,-0.027430033,0.0041767326,0.0074997297,-0.0033281744,0.055964258,-0.02284635,-0.0266552,0.0048385113,0.0019435508,0.046752688,0.0009977092,0.010646459,0.13741435,0.00498649,0.0014687537,-0.035077322,0.03692366,0.00044631306,-0.02737713,-0.05001006,-0.010554855,-0.014740741],"hash":"2627bc38:2145","model":"nomic-embed-text:latest","archived":true},{"uri":"file:///f%3A/blackrockmu/.novamind/memory/session-log.md","text":"## 2026-11-15T20:49:33.823Z\n- **User:** qual a diferenca do injectc1attack para o injectskillc1?\n- **Outcome:** A diferença é o **pipeline de criptografia** aplicado ao mesmo plaintext: ## `InjectC1Attack` (PacketSniffer.cpp:1677) **Aceita:** `0x11` (normal) **e** `0x19` (skill) **Pipeline (2 camadas):** ``` plaintext → XorData[3,len) → Layer-1 → wire (C1 puro) ``` O pacote sai no wire como **C1** — o mesmo caminho do ataque normal. ## `InjectSkillC1` (PacketSniffer.cpp:1704) **Aceita:** só `0x19` (skill) **Pipeline (5 etapas):** ``` plaintext → XorData[3,7) → [serial + payload] → SimpleModulus (6→11) → C3 0D [11] → Layer-1 → wire ``` O pacote sai no wire como **C3** — com SM por cima. --- **Resumindo:** | | `InjectC1Attack` | `InjectSkillC1` | |---|---|---| | Subtypes | 0x11 **e** 0x19 | só 0x19 | | Camadas | XorData + Layer-1 | XorData + **SM** + C3 wrapper + Layer-1 | | Wire resultante | **C1** puro | **C3 0D** [11 bytes] | | Serial | não usa | lê e incrementa `0x08793700` | | Log | mínimo | detalhado (XorData, SM input, SM output) | --- **Contexto importante:** pela análise da captura (sessão 2026-11-15 20:32), o caminho **correto** do skill é o mesmo do 0x11 (C1 puro via `InjectC1Attack`). O `InjectSkillC1` (SM → C3) era baseado no misread do \"0xE7C3\". Porém, o código atual em `AttackModule.cpp:207` ainda chama `InjectSkillC1`: ```cpp return PacketSniffer::InjectSkillC1(plain, 7); ``` Se a conclusão da captura está correta, o `SendSkillAttack` deveria chamar `InjectC1Attack` em vez de `InjectSkillC1`. Quer que eu faça essa troca?\n- **Tools:** search_files, read_file","vector":[0.036045797,0.0327416,-0.12886266,-0.056054384,0.050813816,-0.07440582,0.046708453,0.035962876,-0.094175555,-0.018763568,-0.057265002,-0.026017537,0.07714131,-0.032636616,0.032204617,-0.05578281,-0.011345363,-0.065077305,-0.041137982,0.04251004,0.0146332765,-0.05176763,-0.038526542,-0.033809967,0.100176394,0.032845426,-0.017609293,0.03185423,-0.071988024,-0.024655167,0.04488333,-0.013252993,-0.017586272,-0.06996271,-0.025913505,-0.017413313,0.026489357,-0.020599883,-0.021429125,-0.016158175,0.006239152,-0.024931205,0.04327939,-0.018095864,0.004762484,0.033573646,0.03020362,0.043003544,0.039320238,-0.14047657,0.020544803,0.06871318,-0.021835737,-0.0487